    <statement><p>Suppose <m>P = f(t)</m> is the population in
millions in year <m>t</m>.</p>
<p>Which of the statements below best explains
the meaning of the <alert>INVERSE</alert>
function <m>f^{-1}</m>?</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p>The year <m>t</m> in which the population is <m>P</m> million</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>How long it takes to reach <m>P</m> million</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The population change over time</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The population <m>P</m> in millions in year <m>t</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>None of the above</p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><alert> SOLUTION </alert>




The inverse function gives
the year <m>t</m> in which the population is <m>P</m> million



</solution>
